<!--
Signal plan for Swanston St / Faraday St / Monash Rd (SCATS site 4392), from its DTP Traffic Signal
Configuration Data Sheet (DOC/24/46559, 25 Jan 2024, CC BY 4.0; work/smac/sheets/4250-4449/4392.pdf).
Loaded by 04_run.py for every run of this site (base, signed and closure), in place of the plan netconvert
guessed. The guess had two phases and let drivers turn left from Swanston St into Faraday St on green all
the time, so with the closure (when every driver turns there) nobody ever waited.

The sheet's phases (page 2), in the order A, B, C:
  A (pivot)  Swanston St both ways (SG1 to SG4), SB left into Faraday St with them.
             Pedestrians cross Faraday St (P2) and Monash Rd (P1) at the same time.
  B          Tram stop and bike phase: P3 and P4 cross Swanston St, SG9 bikes, trams. No Faraday St car movement.
  C          Swanston St northbound (SG2) and the left turn from Faraday St into Swanston St southbound (SG5).
Timings (pages 5 and 6): P2 walk 15 s, clearance 6 s. P3 and P4 walk 8 s, clearance 15 + 1 s.
A: minimum green 2 s, maximum extension 20 s, yellow 3 s, all red 5.5 s. B: minimum 8 s.
C: minimum 8 s, maximum extension 10 s, yellow 3 s, all red 1.5 s.

SUMO has no pedestrians here, so:
  - Drivers turning left into Faraday St give way to people on P2. They are held for P2's 15 s walk at the
    start of A, then turn for the rest of A. In the street they may filter through gaps in the crowd.
  - B runs every cycle for its walk and clearance (24 s). Near the university and the tram stop the push
    buttons and trams call it almost every cycle.
The real cycle length is set by SCATS minute by minute and is not published. The phase lengths here let
SUMO's delay-based control stretch A and C with traffic, within the sheet's limits.

Links of this junction in the network (same in net.net.xml and net_closed.net.xml):
  0 Swanston St northbound, straight on          (SG2)
  1 Faraday St westbound, left into Swanston St  (SG5)
  2 Swanston St southbound, left into Faraday St (SG3)
  3 Swanston St southbound, straight on          (SG3)
The id is the one netconvert gives the joined junction. Rebuilding the network can change it; 04_run.py
stops with an error if it is missing.
-->
